{
  "analysis": "The LWL/LWR/SWL/SWR implementations have the shift formulas swapped between LWL and LWR (and SWL and SWR). This corrupts unaligned data reads from the WAD file, causing bad allocation sizes. The allocation got worse after the previous "fix" (from 25MB to 420MB), confirming the shifts are wrong. I need to swap them correctly: LWL uses shift=(3-al)*8, LWR uses shift=al*8, SWL uses shift=(3-al)*8 with right-shift mask, SWR uses shift=al*8 with left-shift mask.",
  "plan": "Patch vm.js with the correct little-endian MIPS LWL/LWR/SWL/SWR formulas. Then run syntax check and test the interpreter again to see if Doom progresses past R_Init.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 - <<'PY'
s = open('/app/vm.js').read()

# Fix LWL: shift should be (3-al)*8, not al*8
old_lwl = '''    case 0x22: { // lwl - little-endian: loads upper bytes of register
      const addr = R[rs] + simm;
      const al = addr & 3;
      const w = readU32(addr & ~3);
      const sh = al * 8;
      const mask = (0xffffffff << sh) >>> 0;
      setR(rt, ((R[rt] >>> 0) & (~mask >>> 0)) | ((w << sh) & mask));
      break;
    }'''
new_lwl = '''    case 0x22: { // lwl - little-endian: loads upper bytes of register
      const addr = R[rs] + simm;
      const al = addr & 3;
      const w = readU32(addr & ~3);
      const sh = (3 - al) * 8;
      const mask = (0xffffffff << sh) >>> 0;
      setR(rt, ((R[rt] >>> 0) & (~mask >>> 0)) | ((w << sh) & mask));
      break;
    }'''
s = s.replace(old_lwl, new_lwl)

# Fix LWR: shift should be al*8, not (3-al)*8
old_lwr = '''    case 0x26: { // lwr - little-endian: loads lower bytes of register
      const addr = R[rs] + simm;
      const al = addr & 3;
      const w = readU32(addr & ~3);
      const sh = (3 - al) * 8;
      const mask = 0xffffffff >>> sh;
      setR(rt, ((R[rt] >>> 0) & (~mask >>> 0)) | ((w >>> sh) & mask));
      break;
    }'''
new_lwr = '''    case 0x26: { // lwr - little-endian: loads lower bytes of register
      const addr = R[rs] + simm;
      const al = addr & 3;
      const w = readU32(addr & ~3);
      const sh = al * 8;
      const mask = 0xffffffff >>> sh;
      setR(rt, ((R[rt] >>> 0) & (~mask >>> 0)) | ((w >>> sh) & mask));
      break;
    }'''
s = s.replace(old_lwr, new_lwr)

# Fix SWL: shift should be (3-al)*8, mask should be >>> sh
old_swl = '''    case 0x2a: { // swl - little-endian: stores upper bytes of register
      const addr = R[rs] + simm;
      const al = addr & 3;
      const w = R[rt] >>> 0;
      const sh = al * 8;
      const mask = (0xffffffff << sh) >>> 0;
      writeU32(addr & ~3, ((readU32(addr & ~3) & (~mask >>> 0)) | (w & mask)) >>> 0);
      break;
    }'''
new_swl = '''    case 0x2a: { // swl - little-endian: stores upper bytes of register
      const addr = R[rs] + simm;
      const al = addr & 3;
      const w = R[rt] >>> 0;
      const sh = (3 - al) * 8;
      const mask = 0xffffffff >>> sh;
      writeU32(addr & ~3, ((readU32(addr & ~3) & (~mask >>> 0)) | ((w >>> sh) & mask)) >>> 0);
      break;
    }'''
s = s.replace(old_swl, new_swl)

# Fix SWR: shift should be al*8, mask should be << sh
old_swr = '''    case 0x2e: { // swr - little-endian: stores lower bytes of register
      const addr = R[rs] + simm;
      const al = addr & 3;
      const w = R[rt] >>> 0;
      const sh = (3 - al) * 8;
      const mask = 0xffffffff >>> sh;
      writeU32(addr & ~3, ((readU32(addr & ~3) & (~mask >>> 0)) | (w & mask)) >>> 0);
      break;
    }'''
new_swr = '''    case 0x2e: { // swr - little-endian: stores lower bytes of register
      const addr = R[rs] + simm;
      const al = addr & 3;
      const w = R[rt] >>> 0;
      const sh = al * 8;
      const mask = (0xffffffff << sh) >>> 0;
      writeU32(addr & ~3, ((readU32(addr & ~3) & (~mask >>> 0)) | ((w << sh) & mask)) >>> 0);
      break;
    }'''
s = s.replace(old_swr, new_swr)

open('/app/vm.js','w').write(s)
print('fixed lwl/lwr/swl/swr shifts')
PY
",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
